Package: plugin-hostd
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: omx-clap-host
Suggests: mod-host
Description: supervisor of LV2 and CLAP plugin hosts behind one mod-host socket
 plugin-hostd speaks mod-host's socket protocol to a controller and runs one
 worker process per plugin, or per named pool of plugins, behind it: mod-host
 for LV2 plugins and omx-clap-host for CLAP plugins. A plugin that crashes
 takes down its own worker and nothing else, and the daemon puts it back.
 Audio never passes through the daemon: every worker is a JACK client, as in
 mod-host.
 .
 A format whose worker is not installed refuses its adds; the other format
 is unaffected. mod-host is not packaged by Debian: install it from source
 for LV2 plugins.

Package: plugin-hostd-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: C header declaring the protocol of plugin-hostd
 The verbs plugin-hostd adds to mod-host's protocol, its placement syntax,
 error codes, feedback events, settings and readiness line, declared once in
 plugin-hostd/protocol.h, which the daemon itself is compiled against.
 Include it from a controller rather than spelling the values again;
 pkg-config plugin-hostd gives the flags. The same declaration as JSON, for
 readers that are not C, is /usr/share/plugin-hostd/protocol.json of the
 plugin-hostd package.
